// =============================================================================
// DataShield — complete system architecture
// Eraser diagram-as-code.  Paste into https://app.eraser.io  →  new diagram
//
// 11 services in 4 layers.  Ports are in the node names so they survive export.
//
// CONNECTOR CONVENTION
//   >    solid arrow  = built and working today
//   -->  dotted arrow = designed, not built yet (the roadmap)
//   <>   bidirectional
// If your Eraser version rejects `-->`, swap those three lines to `>` and rely on
// the PLANNED prefix in the label.
// =============================================================================

title DataShield — DPDP consent management and cross-database DSAR engine

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// External actors
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Browser [icon: monitor, color: gray, shape: oval]
Customer Own Systems [icon: cloud, color: gray, shape: oval]

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LAYER 1 — Product surface.  What a paying customer touches.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Layer 1 Product Surface [color: lightblue] {
  CMS Frontend 5173 [icon: react]
  CMS Backend 8100 [icon: python]
  CMS Database 6543 RLS [icon: postgresql, shape: cylinder]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LAYER 2 — Integration bridge.  Wraps the engine, serves the proof console.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Layer 2 Integration Bridge [color: lightgreen] {
  FastAPI Gateway 8000 [icon: server]
  Access Package JSON [icon: file-text, shape: document]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LAYER 3 — Privacy engine (Ethyca Fides, Apache 2.0).
// Brain and hands are separate processes: a DSAR can take minutes, so the API
// queues it instead of blocking.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Layer 3 Privacy Engine Fides [color: orange] {
  Fides Server 8090 Brain [icon: shield]
  Fides Worker Hands [icon: cpu]
  Fides Redis Queue 7379 [icon: redis, shape: cylinder]
  Fides Database 7432 [icon: postgresql, shape: cylinder]
  Fides Provisioner One Shot [icon: settings]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// LAYER 4 — Customer data.  The DSAR targets: four unrelated engines, three of
// them containers and one a remote SaaS.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Layer 4 Customer Data [color: purple] {
  App Postgres 6432 Users Orders [icon: postgresql, shape: cylinder]
  App Mongo 37017 Events [icon: mongodb, shape: cylinder]
  App MySQL 6306 Support Tickets [icon: mysql, shape: cylinder]
  Zoho CRM SaaS Contacts [icon: cloud]
}

// Built, running, and connected to nothing. Drawn unattached on purpose: an
// arrow here would claim an integration that does not exist yet.
Layer 5 Not Yet Wired [color: gray] {
  Presidio 8001 PII Detection [icon: search]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// BUILT — solid arrows
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Browser > CMS Frontend 5173: 21 screens, 4 roles
Browser > FastAPI Gateway 8000: DSAR proof console at /ui
Browser > Fides Server 8090 Brain: Fides admin UI

CMS Backend 8100 > CMS Database 6543 RLS: tenant-scoped txn, SET LOCAL app.tenant_id

FastAPI Gateway 8000 > Fides Server 8090 Brain: login, token, POST /privacy-request
Fides Server 8090 Brain > Fides Redis Queue 7379: queue job, answer 202 at once
Fides Redis Queue 7379 > Fides Worker Hands: worker picks it up
Fides Server 8090 Brain <> Fides Database 7432: config, requests, execution logs
Fides Provisioner One Shot > Fides Server 8090 Brain: loads /fides-config, verifies, exits 0

// THE ARROWS THAT ARE THE WHOLE PRODUCT.
// One request reaches every engine because every dataset declares identity email.
// The DSR policy targets DATA CATEGORIES, never table names — which is why MySQL
// and Zoho were both added later without touching the policy.
Fides Worker Hands > App Postgres 6432 Users Orders: identity email
Fides Worker Hands > App Mongo 37017 Events: identity email
Fides Worker Hands > App MySQL 6306 Support Tickets: identity email
Fides Worker Hands > Zoho CRM SaaS Contacts: identity email, SaaS connector

Fides Worker Hands > Access Package JSON: writes the access package
Access Package JSON > FastAPI Gateway 8000: read back to serve GET /dsar

FastAPI Gateway 8000 > App Postgres 6432 Users Orders: direct seed and where-is-my-data
FastAPI Gateway 8000 > App Mongo 37017 Events: direct seed and where-is-my-data
FastAPI Gateway 8000 > App MySQL 6306 Support Tickets: direct seed and where-is-my-data
FastAPI Gateway 8000 > Zoho CRM SaaS Contacts: read-only, where-is-my-data

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// PLANNED — dotted arrows.  This is the roadmap, and it is the honest part of
// the diagram: the three pieces are not joined up yet.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CMS Frontend 5173 --> CMS Backend 8100: PLANNED - today runs on in-memory mock data
CMS Backend 8100 --> FastAPI Gateway 8000: PLANNED - DSAR execution and proof
Customer Own Systems --> CMS Backend 8100: PLANNED - public API, key scopes, valid consent right now
